    "summary": "Model passes all L1/L2/L3 checks after repairing one accepted decision.\n\nRoot cause: the accepted decision girder.A held the SINGLE-girder cross-sectional area (1.1389 m²) instead of the merged spine-beam area. Per rule MR-02, for precast girders merged into a single 2D spine beam, A and I must be the single mid-girder section multiplied by the number of girders: A = 1.1389 × 3 = 3.4168 m². The value was inconsistent with girder.w (= γ·A = 88.836 kN/m) and girder.I (= I_single × 3 = 1.0648 m⁴), which broke L2-1 (component params must match provenance decisions / formulas) and L3-2 (total self-weight = γ × A × L).\n\nRepair: re-proposed girder.A = 3.41678625 m² with evidence MR-02 + dec:girder.single.A + INPUT:girder.count_per_span. Since it is a structural decision, re-ran the modal analysis (f1 = 3.4017 Hz, unchanged, so lane.mu = 0.2006 remains valid). Regenerated the model successfully.\n\nModel summary:\n- Structure: simply supported single 30 m span, spine_beam_2d idealization, 3 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40) merged into one beam: A = 3.4168 m², I = 1.0648 m⁴, Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³.\n- Dead load: girder self-weight only, w = 88.84 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m.\n- Supports: two abutments with plain laminated elastomeric bearings (6 per line = 2 per girder end; 300×400 mm, 5 × 8 mm layers), modeled as vertical springs Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, longitudinal springs Kh = 18000 kN/m, rotation free.\n- Live load: Highway Class II, two design lanes, carriageway 9 m; qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 240 kN, ξ = 1.0, μ = 0.2006.\n\nResults: vertical frequencies 3.402 / 13.485 / 29.876 Hz; self-weight reactions 1332.5 kN per abutment; self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m; lane (live-load) midspan moment 6449.6 kN·m."
